/target
# Each crate under crates/unsafe/ is its own workspace with its own build.
crates/unsafe/*/target
# A cargo run from inside a crate's directory builds there; 0.0.200 committed
# one such tree by accident (crates/nikaia/target/floor), removed in 0.0.227.
crates/*/target
/vendor

# Dependencies of the TextMate grammar's scope test (editors/test). The lockfile
# beside it is committed: it pins the version of the reference implementation the
# test's result means anything against.
node_modules/

# Subagent git worktrees (created by the agent harness, never part of the project).
.claude/worktrees/

# Stray build artifacts that were committed once at the repository root.
/hello_world
/hello_world.rs
/check_rustc.rs

# A stray rustc invocation without `-o` leaves one of these.
/a.out

# What `nikaia --input examples/x.nika` leaves beside the source it lowered: the
# Rust, and the ledger of the one file it was pointed at. A project build writes
# both into its own output directory, and a package's real ledger is committed
# ([ADR-020](docs/specification/adr/adr-020.md)) - so these are listed by the
# three directories where a bare `--input` is run by hand, and nowhere wider.
# The committed Rust under `benches/*/src/` is not matched: a generated file
# lands *beside* the `.nika` it came from, never in a `src/`.
/examples/*.rs
/examples/nikaia.contracts
/examples/nikaia.derived
# What `nikaia test` or `nikaia run` leaves inside an example package: the build
# and the lockfile of a run in place, which is how `tests/examples.rs` runs them
# (#534): its builds are reused from one run to the next.
/examples/*/target/
/examples/*/nikaia.lock
/benches/*.rs
/benches/nikaia.contracts
/benches/nikaia.derived
/tests/samples/*.rs
/tests/samples/nikaia.contracts
/tests/samples/nikaia.derived
# And in `std`'s own directory of the toolchain's Nikaia, where a module is
# lowered by hand while it is written; `nikaia lower-std` writes the `.rs` that
# is committed, and nothing reads a ledger here (0.0.253 removed the one that
# had been committed by accident at 0.0.169).
/crates/nikaia-std/src/tools/nikaia.contracts
/crates/nikaia-std/src/tools/nikaia.derived

# The documentation site, as `scripts/site-build.sh` builds it, and what the
# build and `wrangler` leave beside it.
/_site/
/.jekyll-cache/
/.sass-cache/
/.wrangler/
/scripts/site-jekyll/Gemfile.lock

# The language package builds in place, so a test run of it reuses its build;
# what a build writes beside it changes with the compiler and is not committed.
/tests/language/target
/tests/language/nikaia.lock
/tests/language/nikaia.contracts
/tests/language/nikaia.derived
/tests/language/nikaia.proofs
/tests/build-time/target
/tests/build-time/nikaia.lock
/tests/build-time/nikaia.contracts
/tests/build-time/nikaia.derived
/tests/build-time/nikaia.proofs
